  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical ladders are arranged as shown in the figure. Mass of the block is <math><mi>m</mi></math> and the mass of each ladder is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>. The length of each of the ladder is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>. The system is in equilibrium. What is the magnitude of frictional force acting at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0103_3af39a740ce6.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 161px;\" />"
  },
